+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static coffee-shop landing page. WebMCP tools are registered by `webmcp.js`,
+loaded with `defer` so the page content is available first.
+
+## Agent tools
+
+| Tool | Input | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `get_seasonal_favorites` | `{}` | Reads the visible featured drinks, descriptions, and details URLs. |
+| `get_navigation_options` | `{}` | Lists named destinations from the page's links. |
+| `navigate_to_page` | `{"page":"menu"}` | Opens an allowed destination in the current tab. |
+
+The live navigation schema enumerates all supported page identifiers. Tools read
+the same DOM content and links used by visitors. Navigation accepts only marked,
+same-origin HTTP(S) links; the logout link is intentionally not exposed.
+Ordering navigation opens the existing order link; it does not place an order.
+The linked routes are existing links in this static site, not routes implemented
+by this integration.
+
+## Browser support
+
+WebMCP requires a secure context and a browser exposing
+`document.modelContext.registerTool`. Availability is experimental; see the
+[Chrome WebMCP documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api)
+for current browser enablement. Unsupported browsers keep the ordinary page and
+links, without loading a polyfill or contacting an MCP server.
+
+Registrations use an AbortSignal for cleanup on page exit and are restored when
+the page returns from the back/forward cache. A failed registration rolls back
+the tools already registered by that attempt.
